SUMMARY:Deadline: Who Let The Docs Out: Documentary Grants\, Autumn 2026 Cy
 cle (animals and food systems)
DESCRIPTION:Who Let The Docs Out funds independent documentary shorts (5 to
  40 minutes)\, features (over 40 minutes) and series in thematic cycles. T
 he AUTUMN 2026 CYCLE supports documentaries that recalibrate our relations
 hip with animals and food systems\, at four stages (up to\, features/serie
 s vs shorts): Research USD 8\,000 / 4\,000\; Development USD 15\,000 / 7\,
 500\; Production USD 50\,000 / 25\,000\;...\n\nOrganisation: Who Let The D
 ocs Out\nLocation: Remote program (monthly virtual sessions)\; documentary
  projects\nAward: Up to\, features/series vs shorts: Research USD 8\,000 /
  4\,000\; Development USD 15\,000 / 7\,500\; Production USD 50\,000 / 25\,
 000\; Post-Production USD 30\,000 / 15\,000. No application fee stated.\nD
 uration: Grants announced and disbursed late February 2027\; awarded filmm
 akers join a programme of monthly virtual sessions.\n\nMore: https://www.d
 ocsout.org/grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://www.docsout.org/grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote program (monthly virtual sessions)\; documentary projects
END:VEVENT
