DESCRIPTION:The Nieman Foundation brings around two dozen journalists to Ha
 rvard each year for two semesters of study\, reflection and community\, on
 e of the oldest and best-known midcareer journalism fellowships in the wor
 ld.\n\nOrganisation: Nieman Foundation for Journalism at Harvard\nLocation
 : Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, USA (residential academic year at Harvard)\n
 Award: USD 87\,500 stipend paid over the nine-month academic year (2026-27
  figure)\, plus additional allowances for housing\, childcare and health i
 nsurance. Fellows audit courses across Harvard and participate in Nieman s
 eminars\, master classes and workshops. No application fee.\nDuration: Two
  semesters in residence at Harvard\, academic year 2027-28\n\nMore: https:
 //nieman.harvard.edu/fellowships/how-to-apply/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
