 ve public services through AI\, especially for underserved communities. FO
 CUS AREAS: public health\, economic mobility\, environmental resilience an
 d civic engagement (projects on voting or elections are excluded).\n\nOrga
 nisation: The Rockefeller Foundation and OpenAI Foundation\, managed by RF
  Catalytic Capital (RFCC)\nLocation: Global call: cities in all regions ar
 e eligible. Organisations headquartered\, registered or operating in a cou
 ntry under comprehensive U.S. OFAC sanctions are excluded.\nAward: USD 50 
 million total. Seed track USD 500\,000 to under 1 million\; Scale track US
 D 1 to 2 million. 24-month grants\, 50 percent at start and 50 percent on 
 a documented mid-term milestone. No application fee stated.\nDuration: 24 
 months.\n\nMore: https://www.rockefellerfoundation.org/cities-deliver-ai-s
 olutions-for-public-services/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
